med at various clubs around the city including Max's Kansas City CBGB and the Mud Club around this time bosia I moved in with Alexis Adler who lived in the East Village section of Lura Manhattan Adler who was a biology graduate at Barnard saw firsthand his creative Explorations he couldn't afford canvases so instead he used the floors walls doors and Furniture to work on he'd also create postcards and sell them around the city for a dollar while selling these postcards in SoHo he saw his Idol Andy Warhol at the WPA restaurant in Manhattan's Spring Street with friend and curator Henry geler geler dismissed young basat initially but Warhol ignored it and bought one of his postcards titled stupid games bad ideas this would be their first encounter but did they know that this would eventually lead into a full-on professional relationship later that year bosia began working on O'Brien's independent film downtown 81 the feature film wouldn't actually get released until the year 2000 almost 20 years later he was","t0":400,"t1":600,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"10":0.06172451649639721,"19":0.048949529166550466,"20":0.035750144050867495,"81":0.05773447567180989,"1979":0.06287333994822805,"2000":0.05408839344296862,"lower":0.05126027235084304,"east":0.18862001984468416,"side":0.040164582661291026,"including":0.08762132978026464,"village":0.09789905833310093,"soho":0.11546895134361979,"around":0.11254374756074038,"school":0.0849506516911672,"visual":0.045303446937709164,"arts":0.045303446937709164,"where":0.04415462348587833,"he":0.17108570809533974,"friend":0.06738075868064834,"fellow":0.0424753258455836,"artist":0.05319561907858041,"keith":0.10817678688593724,"herring":0.10252054470168608,"kenny":0.06287333994822805,"sharf":0.06287333994822805,"hindsight":0.06287333994822805,"legendary":0.06287333994822805,"crew":0.05773447567180989,"considering":0.06287333994822805,"notoriety":0.06287333994822805,"impact":0.03821087713667521,"collectively":0.05773447567180989,"made":0.0308