,"arrange":0.053799577979497276,"lunch":0.049402344913894836,"none":0.04386248641889066,"turn":0.0353117364123414,"nightclub":0.053799577979497276,"called":0.026850986184840844,"factory":0.049402344913894836,"immediately":0.041885225337543505,"hit":0.03748799227194107,"off":0.027312541421134307,"brought":0.03876533882679461,"polaroid":0.053799577979497276,"camera":0.04386248641889066,"began":0.031248219250443278,"taking":0.03748799227194107,"pictures":0.046282458403145946}},{"id":"doc_1785212350055_7ajtlt_c4","text":"young artist then they took a few together then out of nowhere basad decided to leave before they even finish lunch he returned about an hour later with the fresh painting paint still wet of the two together and he named it do cesas visitors and employees flocked around to see the painting and it was easy to say that Warhol was impressed saying I'm really jealous he is faster than me this would officially Mark the beginning of their Infamous relationship the two began to work together frequently and created famous works such as Armen Hammer 2 and Untitled General Electric too it made for a timely combination as Warhol in the early 80s was struggling to maintain relevancy he was considered a hasb been and bosia was a young upand cominging Talent Fresh eyes and a away for Warhol to stay in touch with the new generation unfortunately the relationship was shortlived it all started at the Tony shafrazi gallery show in 1985 the critical reaction to the show was poor with bosia being referred to as warhol's mascot in a New York Times article after the show it became an embarrassment for the pair to even be seen together bosia took a personal as he didn't want people to look at him as just another warhall Protegé eventually he would slowly stop calling warhall and then altogether the two would stop collaborating and the relationship never recovered from there on February 22nd 1987 Andy warhall passed away his heart stopped beating after he had been recovering from gallbladder surgery basad struggled to cope with his death his drug use continue to worson in 1986 his girlfriend Jennifer good was able to get him into a methadone program but he quit after after just 3 weeks in the last months of his life bosot became a recluse despite his attempts of sobriety bosot passed away at his home on August 12th 1988 from a heroin overdose he was found unresponsive in his home by his girlfriend Kelly imman the greatest black contemporary artist of his generation was Gone Too Soon at the young age of 27 his funeral will be held at the Greenwood Cemetery in Brooklyn in the obituary Herring wrote for Vogue he stated he truly created a lifetime of Works in 10 years greedily we wonder what else he might have created what masterpieces we have been cheated out of by his death but the fact is that he has created enough work to Intrigue generations to come only now will people begin to understand the magnitude of his contribution bosia left the world with over a thousand paintings and drawings after his death the New York Times indicated that bosia was the most famous of only a small number of young black artists who have achieved National recognition his stamp on pop culture is unparalleled from references by musicians to his influence and fashion Basia was able to leave his mark in the world","t0":800,"t1":1000,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"10":0.030300460101220002,"27":0.04301316166936222,"1985":0.06172883115716017,"1986":0.06172883115716017,"1987":0.0503271609178194,"1988":0.05668351170189051,"young":0.1403974789809046,"artist":0.05222727774771002,"then":0.06979829126765842,"took":0.06615419952660424,"few":0.0503271609178194,"together":0.13486142816395846,"nowhere":0.05668351170189051,"basad":0.10620760115980307,"decided":0.05668351170189051,"leave":0.08340426068112151,"before":0.023552162304812347,"even":0.045972921705525624,"finish":0.048058481124631874,"lunch":0.05668351170189051,"he":0.21836277564149784,"returned":0.0503271609178194,"