.035981872977325115,"technique":0.05326152269912596,"understanding":0.04890826682737571,"classical":0.039811295689558254,"once":0.02751663992769162,"again":0.029090640802446333,"barcelona":0.041466326760476666,"city":0.03495857999459066,"crucial":0.04581958263222691,"development":0.04342381304422415,"artist":0.02253164596775742,"there":0.013927876156897853,"attended":0.04342381304422415,"elota":0.05326152269912596,"school":0.035981872977325115,"fine":0.03837764256532785,"arts":0.03837764256532785,"prestigious":0.05326152269912596,"institution":0.041466326760476666,"impressed":0.04890826682737571,"teachers":0.05326152269912596,"style":0.03495857999459066,"unmistakable":0.05326152269912596,"proficiency":0.05326152269912596,"far":0.035981872977325115,"beyond":0.03837764256532785,"youthful":0.05326152269912596,"work":0.01639269067757443,"adhered":0.05326152269912596,"something":0.01656727094736157,"brewing":0.05326152269912596,"inside":0.03711307088872643,"wanted":0.03316501216244618,"break":0.03495857999459066,"free":0.035981872977325115,"masters":0.041466326760476666,"drawn":0.04890826682737571,"experimentation":0.10652304539825191,"take":0.02383463074447348,"brink":0.05326152269912596,"took":0.02853993291042607,"dark":0.04342381304422415,"turn":0.03495857999459066,"after":0.02658244662667857,"moving":0.03402438669357762}},{"id":"doc_1785212350168_21tbmo_c1","text":"Paris in 1901 Picasso was living in near poverty struggling to sell his art during this period his friend Carlos casimus took his own life after a failed romantic relationship the shock of Carlos's death deeply affected Picasso casting a shadow over his spirit this marked the beginning of what art historians call the blue period a time when Picasso's paintings were dominated by blue hues representing his Melancholy and grief during this phase his subjects were often the impoverished the lonely and the dispossessed reflecting his own inner struggle one of the most famous works from this period is the old guitarist the painting depicts a blind emaciated man hunched over strumming his guitar his gaunt figure F and tattered clothing capture the sorrow and despair of The Human Condition the blue color pallet conveys a sense of coldness both emotionally and physically as if the world around him has drained of all warmth though Picasso was still quite young this period reflected an emotional maturity far beyond his years he was grappling with the harsh realities of Life portraying human suffering with a level of depth that connected with the viewer's soul during the blue period Picasso lived in in Mont martra Paris an area known for its vibrant Bohemian atmosphere he rented a small Studio that lacked Heating and was frequently cold it was said that Picasso was often hungry sometimes trading paintings for meals his financial struggles during this time mirrored the Desolation in his art but like many of Picasso's phases the blue period would not last forever as the emotional weight of his grief began to lift his art would once again transform little did the world know this was just the beginning around 1904 Picasso's life took on a brighter tone after meeting Fernando leier a model and artist who became his lover Picasso's painting started to shift this new phase known as The Rose period marked a turning point in both Picasso's art and life the works from this period are characterized by warmer colors pinks oranges and reds and reflect themes of love romance and circus life life one of his most famous paintings from this era family of Salim banz shows a group of circus performers acrobats jugglers and musicians standing in a Barren landscape their solitary figures seem distant yet there's a sense of familial Connection in the way they interact with one another although the rose period had a lighter mood compared to the blue period Picasso's subjects were still somewhat melancholic the circus performers often referred to as saltimbank symbolized the artists of the time traveling from town to town Always On The Fringe of society and always putting on a performance during this period Picasso's love for classical art began to surface again while he still painted in his distinctive style he also became more interested in form particularly the human body and how it could be simplified this Fascination would later evolve into something that","t0":200,"t1":400,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"1901":0.04089977438185122,"1904":0.05024546536353235,"paris":0.062225649535992196,"picasso":0.27777219120493835,"living":0.03812777754843789,"near":0.04461106139718715,"poverty":0.04089977438185122,"struggling":0.04089977438185122,"sell":0.029886006592736745,"his":0.3192762446416682,"art":0.1284148358878756,"during":0.15241183880702236,"period":0.3574271094030194,"friend":0.02932024182312034,"carlos":0.09414466720912006,"casimus":0.04707233360456003,"took":0.05864048364624068,"own":0.045673915948742115,"life":0.1193762712543837,"after":0.054618472004864256,"failed":0.04461106139718715,"romantic":0.04461106139718715,"relationship":0.02878208656675674,"shock":0.04461106139718715,"death":0.029886006592736745,"deeply":0.05024546536353235,"affected":0.04707233360456003,"casting":0.05471774339159344,"shadow":0.04707233360456003,"spirit":0.039426923817526605,"marked":0.07885384763505321,"beginning":0.08179954876370243,"historians":0.05471774339159344,"call":0.031781514030493195,"blue":0.22179390966092247,"time":0.054486867127454174,"paintings":0.08965801977821024,"were":0.06502449610826076,"dominated":0.05024546536353235,"hues":0.05471774339159344,"representing":0.05471774339159344,"melancholy":0.05471774339159344,"grief":0.10943548678318687,"phase":0.10943548678318687,"subjects":0.08179954876370243,"often":0.10221532542367132,"impoverished":0.05471774339159344,"lonely":0.05471774339159344,"dispossessed":0.05471774339159344,"reflecting":0.04461106139718715,"inner":0.05024546536353235,"struggle":0.05471774339159344,"most":0.03932765243079743,"famous":0.0762555550968