,"circle":0.0327823355711889,"avant":0.06801393559269947,"garde":0.06801393559269947,"introduced":0.04549620543218809,"carles":0.29244345814824957,"casagemas":0.09099241086437618,"spanish":0.03170213339395507,"poet":0.041777636878321374,"became":0.08498905758068552,"incredibly":0.03709279455018983,"close":0.03073585961969024,"friends":0.054034582131647066,"pablo":0.02586940505002429,"even":0.01694178758145723,"painted":0.028329685860228503,"portraits":0.04549620543218809,"travels":0.041777636878321374,"throughout":0.03709279455018983,"spain":0.03073585961969024,"world":0.014773838085881572,"there":0.011897247445362613,"place":0.03073585961969024,"everyone":0.027650032865850143,"wanted":0.028329685860228503,"featured":0.035420701947821785,"bustling":0.09099241086437618,"french":0.034006967796349735,"capital":0.041777636878321374,"paris":0.07760821515007287,"knowledge":0.035420701947821785,"language":0.041777636878321374,"climate":0.041777636878321374,"terrain":0.04549620543218809,"keenly":0.04549620543218809,"leapt":0.04549620543218809,"visited":0.0327823355711889,"settled":0.035420701947821785,"vacant":0.03913927050168849,"whilst":0.03709279455018983,"attending":0.035420701947821785,"exhibitions":0.03709279455018983,"universal":0.034006967796349735,"raked":0.03913927050168849,"million":0.024378924689190652,"visitors":0.03709279455018983,"pining":0.03913927050168849,"influx":0.03913927050168849,"talent":0.03073585961969024,"time":0.015101412853999654,"both":0.028329685860228503,"infatuated":0.04549620543218809,"women":0.03170213339395507,"resided":0.04549620543218809,"city":0.029861758666497498,"love":0.03902494023904939,"met":0.06147171923938048,"woman":0.06147171923938048,"berthe":0.04549620543218809,"weill":0.09099241086437618,"only":0.021972750929728915,"dealer":0.03709279455018983,"promote":0.041777636878321374,"formed":0.035420701947821785,"working":0.024378924689190652,"relationship":0.023931464311983435,"she":0.02309715135394979,"accepted":0.03709279455018983,"deal":0.03709279455018983,"hand":0.034006967796349735,"laure":0.04549620543218809,"gargallo":0.04549620543218809,"known":0.024378924689190652,"germaine":0.13648861629656428,"immediately":0.035420701947821785,"fell":0.03709279455018983,"spurned":0.04549620543218809,"affections":0.04549620543218809,"doing":0.019512470119524696,"caused":0.041777636878321374,"reach":0.029861758666497498,"terrible":0.041777636878321374,"depression":0.03709279455018983,"mood":0.03709279455018983,"swings":0.04549620543218809,"frequent":0.04549620543218809,"degree":0.03913927050168849,"danger":0.04549620543218809,"herself":0.041777636878321374,"17th":0.041777636878321374,"february":0.0327823355711889,"put":0.02006846571018972,"gun":0.041777636878321374,"temple":0.041777636878321374,"ended":0.03709279455018983,"own":0.018988263532955886,"attendance":0.03913927050168849,"returned":0.03709279455018983,"heartstruck":0.04549620543218809,"news":0.035420701947821785,"friend":0.024378924689190652,"death":0.024849341570247874}},{"id":"doc_1785212350223_0j82g0_c2","text":"he didn't yet realize, this event had transpired into one of Picasso's greatest, yet terrible, inspirations. Following the death of his friend, Pablo Picasso found himself in one of his most depressive, emotionally torn states. &gt;&gt; [music] [music] &gt;&gt; This was known as the Blue Period. Aptly named not only due to the emotional state of Picasso, but the new style of paintings completely bathed in blue. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; His new imagery illustrated his darker, more tortured side. It was an aspect of this artist [music] nobody had seen before. There was a degree of emotional poverty, a bleak, radical [music] outlook on the world. His brushstrokes were fluid, emphasizing [music] his raw emotion, generating an aesthetic which remains emotionally resonating to the eye. His work, though visually bleak, still depicted the resilience of the human spirit. From downtrodden beggars to brothel workers. This was a [music] time of anti-commercialism. Pablo did not sell many paintings to the public as this particular aesthetic was seen as [music] self-deprecating and rudimentary. &gt;&gt; It's a portrait of friend of Picasso, uh Angel Fernandez [music] de Soto, and it's a momento of a moment [music] of moulin lived between Barcelona and Paris together by the two artists. There's never been a better period to present [music] this work on the market. It's a seminal work. It's a masterpiece and we have a masterpiece [music] driven market at the moment. So, we expect interest globally from all our clients internationally. &gt;&gt; The Old Guitarist is one of Pablo [music] Picasso's most famous works. It depicts a blind, emaciated old man hunched over his guitar sitting in a desolate environment. The continued use of blue sets a melodramatic tone for the painting conveying a sense of sadness, despair, and isolation reflecting the emotional state of the subject alongside the artist himself during this period of his life. The composition is simple, yet powerful with the old guitarist occupying much of the canvas. His elongated, thin figure and hunched posture suggest physical frailty and emotional burden. The way he cradles the guitar in his arms emphasizes his connection [music] to music, perhaps as a source of solace or escape from his harsh reality. This painting has been interpreted as a symbol of human suffering and endurance, particularly in the face of poverty and adversity. His blindness [music] could symbolize a lack of hope or insight into a better future. The guitar, a recurring [music] motif in Picasso's work, may represent the arts as a form of spiritual refuge or as a means of [music] expression for the marginalized. The Blue Period coincided with a personal and artistic transition as well as broader social and political upheaval [music] in Europe. The destitute figure of the old guitarist can be seen as a commentary on the plight of the poor who were often overlooked or forgotten by society. While Picasso's style is unmistakably [music] modern, The Old Guitarist also shows the influence of earlier masters such as","t0":400,"t1":600,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"he":0.02997370957368893,"didn":0.026599443813572297,"yet":0.10555073967666667,"realize":0.03968514893252238,"event":0.044903239821065394,"had":0.03780792142076206,"transpired":0.05507611513890492,"picasso":0.16309501217597194,"greatest":0.035183579892222226,"terrible":0.05057454609860474,"inspirations":0.05507611513890492,"following":0.04116764587474106,"death":0.030081743838809787,"his":0.2646554499453344,"friend":0.05902454722936574,"pablo":0.0939497910369961,"found":0.035183579892222226,"himself":0.07036715978444445,"most":0.03958522737167938,"depressive":0.05507611513890492,"emotionally":0.10114909219720948,"torn":0.05507611513890492,"states":0.05507611513890492,"gt":0.21229925370331681,"music":0.4536467578007146,"known":0.02951227361468287,"blue":0.14883102687149652,"period":0.1308247507102959,"aptly":0.04738063203571365,"named":0.03720775671787413,"only":0.026599443813572297,"due":0.044903239821065394,"emotional":0.17961295928426158,"state":0.08233529174948212,"style":0.0722992013484545,"paintings":0.06016348767761957,"completely":0.04287906299541348,"bathed":0.05507611513890492,"imagery":0.05507611513890492,"illustrated":0.05057454609860474,"darker":0.05507611513890492,"tortured":0.05507611513890492,"side":0.035183579892222226,"aspect":0.044903239821065394,"artist":0.04659857490742055,"nobody":0.035183579892222226,"seen":0.09024523151642935,"before":0.02101386950884389,"there":0.028804783340161736,"degree":0.04738063203571365,"poverty":0.08233529174948212,"bleak":0.11015223027780983,"radical":0.04738063203571365,"outlook":0.05507611513890492,"world":0.017884691695318356,"brushstrokes":0.05507611513890492,"were":0.04363358102298321,"fluid":0.05507611513890492,"emphasizing":0.05507611513890492,"raw":0.044903239821065394,"emotion":0.03968514893252238,"generating":0.055076115138904