 end. &gt;&gt; The new movement had departed from the conventional [music] Western artistry, and swayed towards capturing life in a new avant-garde manner, through geometric shapes and facets. Alongside the art being fragmented and multi-dimensional, it also paved the way for displaying philosophical connotations within the paint. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Artists could now represent the concept of time in a new manner. Cubism was so significant that it had crossed into other disciplines. Gertrude Stein herself [music] derived principles from Cubism in her literary work, which merged into the Dada movement. A new age of counterculture had begun. &gt;&gt; But he was enchanting. Oh, the children just ogled eyed, you know. &gt;&gt; Did you feel something very [music] special around? &gt;&gt; Oh, yes. No question. He was He was He was supposed to be in his 80s. He was a bit frail. I mean, &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; lent on his son's shoulder. Um but he was loving. He really was. He's like a star actor, you know. [music] He came on the stage and you couldn't see anybody else. It was like seeing Olivier doing something wonderful. But what I loved about him and what I loved about his work [music] in this particular area which he did what in the last 20 years of his life or more or perhaps um is the humor. I mean, people [music] say oh, it's so very simple and elementary. They're idiots. They're They're pompous. They're stupid. His humor, his sense of humor and joy and happiness [music] and immediate rapport with children. My two daughters and Michael through my son just thought it was the greatest thing since sliced bread. Uh these sort of humor pieces of art, if you want to call it that, which it is, of course, and a very particular form of his art. &gt;&gt; Picasso bought his first painting in 1908, a portrait of a woman made in 1895 by French artist [music] Henri Rousseau. Picasso, delighted with his purchase, celebrated the works of [music] Henri by organizing a banquet at the Bateau-Lavoir. In attendance [music] was Guillaume Apollinaire, Marie Laurencin, Andre Salmon, Georges Braque, and Gertrude Stein. Picasso did [music] what any great artist should and developed upon preconceived ideas, to be inspired by the works of old and transform it into his own voice. &gt;&gt; A call","t0":1200,"t1":1400,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"20":0.032221890802510936,"1895":0.048750301669352084,"1908":0.05203654474763274,"because":0.017815766356935867,"he":0.26214155930858973,"knew":0.03828335094958183,"ultimately":0.05203654474763274,"before":0.02162133415663097,"went":0.035286317659511235,"birthday":0.05666824422632762,"brought":0.04083235911237654,"me":0.07203102814105866,"photograph":0.11333648845265525,"signed":0.05666824422632762,"music":0.396746582777174,"gave":0.04083235911237654,"said":0.10810667078315485,"asked":0.035286317659511235,"name":0.02828271707670612,"know":0.06421950375874869,"work":0.05232360727411251,"richard":0.05666824422632762,"attenborough":0.05666824422632762,"very":0.08340376202139309,"difficult":0.05666824422632762,"yes":0.05961613947547617,"gt":0.43687271433668695,"spelled":0.05666824422632762,"him":0.050718289963359434,"est":0.05666824422632762,"sophie":0.05666824422632762,"monsieur":0.05666824422632762,"sorry":0.048750301669352084,"there":0.01481873306686527,"end":0.07438921189429624,"ll":0.02273667562384081,"capital":0.05203654474763274,"letter":0.04620129350655737,"movement":0.07897380542392464,"had":0.058351297636680434,"departed":0.05666824422632762,"conventional":0.048750301669352084,"western":0.05666824422632762,"artistry":0.05203654474763274,"swayed":0.05666824422632762,"towards":0.0423577117734085,"capturing":0.04620129350655737,"life":0.04121054265620578,"avant":0.0423577117734085,"garde":0.0423577117734085,"manner":0.10407308949526548,"through":0.052241944642008334,"geometric":0.048750301669352084,"shapes":0.04083235911237654,"facets":0.05203654474763274,"alongside":0.03620065963368166,"art":0.066496193