"got":0.02732992634092235,"broad":0.05475919927970735,"valuation":0.05475919927970735,"very":0.060445536396444,"powerful":0.07891358979696066,"expressive":0.05028353291276287,"work":0.03370728323389185,"snorts":0.05028353291276287,"painted":0.068195177985293,"subject":0.04464486014427161,"jacqueline":0.17857944057708644,"there":0.01431951824447501,"lot":0.021691253572431086,"influences":0.05475919927970735,"time":0.036352098730952576,"um":0.26917784256504507,"looking":0.08487116550273606,"particularly":0.04464486014427161,"delacroix":0.05028353291276287,"les":0.04464486014427161,"femmes":0.047107997089093835,"alger":0.047107997089093835,"ingres":0.05028353291276287,"artists":0.04973357879220026,"uh":0.2784429418713953,"old":0.02562835695961708,"period":0.03251799158671364,"provided":0.05028353291276287,"endless":0.05028353291276287,"source":0.03498112853153586,"fascination":0.047107997089093835,"throughout":0.04464486014427161,"life":0.03982223816081507,"matisse":0.17052932288859748,"were":0.021691253572431086,"great":0.04451489396656077,"sparring":0.05475919927970735,"partners":0.05028353291276287,"20th":0.0381566643552049,"century":0.0369936579536581,"just":0.013633685807951764,"died":0.04093076134084409,"felt":0.04263233072214937,"left":0.0369936579536581,"hole":0.05028353291276287,"terms":0.04464486014427161,"competition":0.04093076134084409,"historical":0.05028353291276287,"discussion":0.05475919927970735,"him":0.04900968761511886,"picture":0.08186152268168818,"much":0.05125671391923416,"paean":0.047107997089093835,"last":0.0293424557630446,"longest":0.047107997089093835,"lasting":0.04263233072214937,"muse":0.04464486014427161,"marry":0.047107997089093835,"years":0.022551820467321716,"after":0.02732992634092235,"tribute":0.1095183985594147,"masters":0.04263233072214937,"past":0.0381566643552049,"relationship":0.02880389278328612,"incredibly":0.04464486014427161,"strong":0.0381566643552049,"character":0.04464486014427161,"think":0.0174011100844462,"length":0.05475919927970735,"alongside":0.03498112853153586,"talents":0.05028353291276287,"painter":0.04093076134084409,"multilingual":0.05475919927970735,"profound":0.05028353291276287,"ability":0.0381566643552049,"communicate":0.05028353291276287,"multitude":0.05475919927970735,"cultures":0.05028353291276287,"apparent":0.05475919927970735,"attempting":0.05028353291276287,"strip":0.05475919927970735,"away":0.027799714322761505,"bonds":0.047107997089093835,"many":0.02063918631029851,"tied":0.05475919927970735,"tradition":0.047107997089093835,"wanted":0.0340975889926465,"unlearn":0.05475919927970735,"seek":0.05475919927970735,"own":0.022854259973977883,"interpretation":0.05028353291276287,"audiences":0.05475919927970735,"saw":0.0369936579536581,"convention":0.05475919927970735,"nature":0.047107997089093835,"quickly":0.03945679489848033,"sculpture":0.04093076134084409,"since":0.04464486014427161,"wasn":0.0340975889926465,"taught":0.03594159069152553,"form":0.03251799158671364,"academic":0.05028353291276287,"sense":0.03180559270786682,"artist":0.023165220014794857,"moving":0.03498112853153586}},{"id":"doc_1785212350223_0j82g0_c8","text":"on occasion to suit his needs. He continued to develop on Cubism, working alongside Braque [music] on Analytic Cubism to Synthetic, effectively incorporating real-world materials into their artwork [music] to create depth in its messaging. The guitar series are some notable works from the period. &gt;&gt; The city of Chicago gets its own Picasso in a king-size piece of sculpture five stories high at the Civic Center Plaza, but not everyone likes it. Pickets call it the colossal boo-boo, among other things. It weighs 163 tons and cost $300,000 to construct. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; The official unveiling triggers an assortment of comments, some praising it, others condemning it. They range from sophisticated and genteel to just a big homely thing. Even the hippies stare. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Untitled, the Chicago Picasso resembles a woman's head in profile. The crowd starts tossing more than just opinions as everyone agrees whatever it is, Chicago's got it. &gt;&gt; On the 3rd of May, 1913, Picasso's greatest inspiration, his father, Pepe, passed away. Picasso's response to his father's death was to delve deeper into his art, pushing boundaries and exploring new techniques and styles. His father's passing seemed to catalyze a period of intense creativity and innovation in his work. The artist's personal life also underwent changes. He became involved with different romantic partners and moved through various social [music] circles in Europe, all of which influenced his work. It was his relentless pursuit of truth and authenticity that continues to inspire artists today. His demeanor was noted to be incredibly self-assured, often referring [music] to himself as a genius, which to his respect he was. He had a larger-than-life persona and a reputation for being somewhat egotistical, which might have led to perceptions of grandiosity. Such pride derived from his innate belief that he was indeed born [music] to leave a lasting impact on the world. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; We all think we know Picasso, but a new exhibition at Tate [music] Britain is inviting us to think again and to re-examine his relationship with Britain. &gt;&gt; Actually, early on Britain was supposed to be an influence on him as a, you know, in growing up. His father was a great Anglophile and was known as El Inglés because of his passion for all things English and Picasso told [music] his biographer Roland Penrose that he was on his way to London in 1900 when he [music] stopped off in Paris and and never carried on or finished the journey. And the reason was partly his admiration for British painting. [music] &gt;&gt; The exhibition also examines the impact of Picasso's later influence on British artists. [music] &gt;&gt; Picasso kind of shows how much more is really looking at at that Renaissance classical [music] tradition and then distorting it and abstracting it. &gt;&gt; There are about a dozen works by Picasso, including the most important, uh a portrait of Serge Lifar executed by Picasso in 1960, estimated [music] at uh 300 to 500,000 francs.","t0":1600,"t1":1800,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"163":0.05470602245431435,"300":0.08518186067158005,"500":0.040891013353699386,"1900":0.044601505384453816,"1913":0.05470602245431435,"1960":0.040891013353699386,"occasion":0.05470602245431435,"suit":0.050234702420626075,"his":0.31920785335565766,"needs":0.040891013353699386,"he":0.10420303768605173,"continued":0.03406447672000492,"develop":0.03695773329961776,"cubism":0.06989431650190793,"working":0.029313961214781702,"alongside":0.034947158250953965,"braque":0.044601505384453816,"music":0.33794880488550894,"analytic":0.050234702420626075,"synthetic":0.050234702420626075,"effectively":0.050234702420626075,"incorporating":0.047062250369478295,"real":0.026420704635168858,"world":0.03552902534991792,"materials":0.044601505384453816,"artwork":0.044601505384453816,"create":0.026853216229757233,"depth":0.047062250369478295,"messaging":0.050234702420626075,"guitar":0.047062250369478295,"series":0.04259093033579003,"some":0.03713375212879753,"notable":0.03695773329961776,"works":0.05460677233223582,"period":0.06497282653185898,"gt":0.4217453504422589,"city":0.03590668770321142,"chicago":0.16411806736294307,"gets":0.03811961030210176,"own":0.02283206613242964,"picasso":0.23142724199002795,"king":0.05470602245431435,"size":0.04259093033579003,"piece":0.034947158250953965,"sculpture":0.040891013353699386,"five":0.03695773329961776,"stories":0.044601505384453816,"high":0.033247241268863324,"civic":0.05470602245431435,"center":0.03941847828464223,"plaza":0.05470602245431435,"everyone":0.06649448253772665,"likes":0.05470602245431435,"pickets":0.05470602245431435,"call":0.03177470619980618,"colossal":0.05470602245431435,"boo":0.1094120449086287,"among":0.05470602245431435,"things":0.0393192281625637,"weighs":0.05470