852141,"constant":0.048492767590399936,"innovation":0.03805160604354505,"teetering":0.05280904046090303,"between":0.03135991679933934,"styles":0.04111405038172095,"chronicled":0.05280904046090303,"struggles":0.04543032325222405,"early":0.03567618966984243,"20th":0.03679777751121786,"century":0.03567618966984243,"works":0.02635661596436297,"message":0.03805160604354505,"peace":0.04543032325222405,"less":0.030672888834866067,"pertinent":0.05280904046090303,"today":0.02635661596436297,"neoclassicism":0.048492767590399936,"prevalent":0.04543032325222405,"once":0.027282872844215794,"projects":0.048492767590399936,"significantly":0.05280904046090303,"cubism":0.03373533317304196,"style":0.034661590052894785,"due":0.04305490687852141,"stricter":0.05280904046090303,"line":0.03567618966984243,"focus":0.032094362386646924,"precise":0.05280904046090303,"human":0.030027525263012222,"anatomy":0.04111405038172095,"took":0.02829747246116344,"great":0.021464784616235896,"deal":0.04305490687852141,"interest":0.03679777751121786,"greek":0.048492767590399936,"mythology":0.05280904046090303,"often":0.03288325944165511,"depicting":0.048492767590399936,"minotaur":0.10561808092180607,"believe":0.02941906030253887,"image":0.04111405038172095,"representative":0.05280904046090303}},{"id":"doc_1785212350223_0j82g0_c10","text":"of mankind, the duality of viciousness as seen in the head of the bull, and tenderness in the human torso. Many believe the bull was also a reference to Picasso's early days of painting bullfighting. It was seen as a nod to the past, but marked a significant point in Picasso's career. He truly became a master of styles. Picasso had later discovered the Romanesque paintings in the Catalan Art Museum. Romanesque art played a crucial role in shaping his artistic vision, and soon political undertones started to appear in his work. 1935 was a moment of clarity for the now 53-year-old artist. He put painting aside and began to write poetry. He also chose to separate from his spouse at the time, Olga, who remained with their son, Paulo Picasso. Picasso was a known womanizer, having cheated on most of the lovers in his life. It is greatly argued as to whether Picasso celebrated his peers in a positive manner or simply wanting to bleed them for his artistic benefits using their figures as a means to an end. It was known that many of his close relations would commonly refer to him as God and on other occasions, the devil. &gt;&gt; There may be little things [music] that have been shown, but not as a whole. This is a really complete presentation. It's eroticism. It's this rather lively period of my grandfather's life, which is not so well known to the public. My grandfather was a bulimic, bulimic and excessive, [music] and I think that's where we find him. &gt;&gt; We know Picasso, the great lady eater, [music] all the women, all the muses he loved, we know that each woman in his life enabled him to imagine [music] to imagine to exercise his imagination and to come up with [music] all his series. Picasso is first and foremost a draftsman to draw a woman's body without looking at it, without a model. &gt;&gt; Being there is a magical few moments to be spent &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; looking at this genius' work. &gt;&gt; It's called Les Femmes d'Alger. He painted it in 1955 &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; and it is simply the single most important work by Picasso remaining in private hands. Uh Picasso is fascinated with Les Femmes d'Alger of Delacroix. Matisse always has been as well. [music] Matisse dies and Picasso, over a period of 2 months, starts his Herculean project of Les Femmes d'Alger, 80 [music] studies on paper, 14 studies in oil, with and without color, looking on its form and color, looking at changing the persons around the figurines from the from the Delacroix initial painting. And he finally arrives at the total resolution of that project, which is the painting behind me. It's really, really uh a phenomenally important painting. It's estimated at around $140 million, which is which in itself is already the most expensive work of art ever sold at auction. &gt;&gt; I mean, it's one of the great Picassos, period.","t0":2000,"t1":2200,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"14":0.041689494018793925,"53":0.05146960815549499,"80":0.05493915886084268,"140":0.05493915886084268,"1935":0.05982921592919322,"1955":0.05146960815549499,"mankind":0.05982921592919322,"duality":0.05982921592919322,"viciousness":0.05982921592919322,"seen":0.06535563167880373,"head":0.04311000038179676,"bull":0.10987831772168535,"tenderness":0.05982921592919322,"human":0.03401923756047247,"torso":0.05982921592919322,"many":0.04510023340751441,"believe":0.033329886245095704,"reference":0.04657955108714446,"picasso":0.27841032473034016,"early":0.04041880777720451,"days":0.04877841555090273,"painting":0.14684003699457018,"bullfighting":0.05493915886084268,"nod":0.05982921592919322,"past":0.041689494018793925,"marked":0.04311000038179676,"significant":0.04877841555090273,"point":0.03552875070885398,"career":0.04877841555090273,"he":0.09768137446297838,"truly":0.04657955108714446,"became":0.0372545990690175,"master":0.04877841555090273,"styles":0.04657955108714446,"had":0.020535383521621046,"later":0.03401923756047247,"discovered":0.05146960815549499,"romanesque":0.11965843185838644,"paintings":0.032677815839401866,"catalan":0.05982921592919322,"art":0.0702053709512808,"museum":0.044720437672928715,"played":0.05493915886084268,"crucial":0.05146960815549499,"role":0.05146960815549499,"shaping":0.05982921592919322,"his":0.22588921873783152,"artistic":0.08622000076359353,"vision":0.04657955108714446,"soon":0.03926933225115366,"political":0.04657955108714446,"undertones":0.05982921592919322,"started":0.03926933225115366,"appear":0.05146960815549499,"work":0.07365631176182412,"moment":0.0372545990690175,"clarity":0.05146960815549499,"now":0.019218400237846524,"year":0.033329886245095704,"old":0.02800122212553227,"artist":0.02531002952094001,"put":0.026390784834400317,"aside":0.05493915886084268,"began":0.03475039260809854,"write":0.03401923756047247,"poetry":0.04877841555090273,"chose":0.05493915886084268,"separate":0.05493915886084268,"spouse":0.05982921592919322,"time":0.01985892409916495,"olga":0.05493915886084268,"remained":0.04657955108714446,"son":0.044720437672928715,"paulo":0.05982921592919322,"known":0.09617760001051887,"womanizer":0.05982921592919322,"having":0.038219943313446234,"cheated":0.05493915886084268,"most":0.06450218329814936,"lovers":0.05493915886084268,"life":0.0652639186761287,"greatly":0.05982921592919322,"argued":0.05982921592919322,"whether":0.04311000038179676,"celebrated":0.05146960815549499,"peers":0.05146960815549499,"positive":0.04877841555090273,"manner":0.05493915886084268,"simply":0.09755683110180546,"wanting":0.05146960815549499,"bleed":0.05982921592919322,"benefits":0.05982921592919322,"figures":0.04311000038179676,"means":0.0372545990690175,"end":0.03926933225115366,"close":0.04041880777720451,"relations":0.05493915886084268,"commonly":0.05982921592919322,"refer":0.05982921592919322,"him":0.08032105714246277,"god":0.04311000038179676,"occasions":0.05982921592919322,"devil":0.05982921592919322,"gt":0.3459312042812374,"there":0.03129065290654103,"little":0.024970278471397475,"things":0.021500727766049783,"music":0.22175853165775164,"shown":0.05493915886084268,"whole":0.03636082989923049,"really":0.060916966031399546,"complete":0.044720437672928715,"presentation":0.04877841555090273,"eroticism":0.05982921592919322,"rather":0.04877841555090273,"lively":0.05982921592919322,"period":0.10658625212656195,"grandfather":0.10987831772168535,"well":0.04201679925043161,"public":0.041689494018793925,"bulimic":0.11965843185838644,"excessive":0.05982921592919322,"think":0.01901223513755436,"where":0.021008399625215807,"find":0.03475039260809854,"know":0.03390084349448357,"great":0.04863641613140729,"lady":0.05146960815549499,"eater":0.05982921592919322,"women":0.041689494018793925,"muses":0.05982921592919322,"loved":0.04877841555090273,"woman":0.08083761555440902,"enabled":0.05982921592919322,"imagine":0.09755683110180546,"exercise":0.04877841555090273,"imagination":0.04877841555090273,"come":0.02757800801154475,"series":0.04657955108714446,"first":0.026773685714154255,"foremost":0.05493915886084268,"draftsman":0.05493915886084268,"draw":0.04877841555090273,"body":0.041689494018793925,"without":0.13416131301878614,"looking":0.12363889790982173,"model":0.05146960815549499,"being":0.02531002952094001,"magical":0.05146960815549499,"few":0.04877841555090273,"moments":0.05493915886084268,"spent":0.05982921592919322,"genius":0.038219943313446234,"called":0.029860335539748012,"les":0.1463352466527082,"femmes":0.154408824466485,"alger":0.154408824466485,"painted":0.0372545990690175,"single":0.03475039260809854,"important":0.061819448954910865,"remaining":0.04877841555090273,"private":0.041689494018793925,"hands":0.04311000038179676,"uh":0.0468035806341872,"fascinated":0.05493915886084268,"delacroix":0.10987831772168535,"matisse":0.09315910217428892,"always":0.028439829176745174,"dies":0.05493915886084268,"months":0.04657955108714446,"starts":0.04877841555090273,"herculean":0.05493915886084268,"project":0.08944087534585743,"studies":0.10987831772168535,"paper":0.04877841555090273,"oil":0.04311000038179676,"color":0.07643988662689247,"form":0.03552875070885398,"changing":0.05493915886084268,"persons":0.05493915886084268,"around":0.05354737142830851,"figurines":0.05982921592919322,"initial":0.05982921592919322,"finally":0.04657955108714446,"arrives":0.05982921592919322,"total":0.05493915886084268,"resolution":0.05493915886084268,"behind":0.041689494018793925,"me":0.01901223513755436,"phenomenally":0.05982921592919322,"estimated":0.04657955108714446,"million":0.03205920000350629,"itself":0.03926933225115366,"already":0.041689494018793925,"expensive":0.05146960815549499,"ever":0.033329886245095704,"sold":0.041689494018793925,"auction":0.05493915886084268,"mean":0.029860335539748012,"picassos":0.05146960815549499}},{"id":"doc_1785212350223_0j82g0_c11","text":"And it's one of the, you know, last great Picassos which has been in private hands. In terms of Picasso's quality at the absolutely top end. And therefore, you know, naturally, it's enormously important. And it's also uh it's the culmination, it's the end of a series of 15 paintings that he did. And it's a large painting as well. So, in all those dimensions, it's an extremely important piece. When a major work of art by a major artist comes up, There's sufficient global interest and the various economies are still strong enough to mean that they're pushed to to price levels which we haven't seen before. This is a masterpiece. I mean, it really is a masterpiece. So, I think it will undoubtedly it'll make a very substantial price. And yes, will it break record? I think it's perfectly possible that it'll break records. &gt;&gt; Now, the conventional view, I have to admit, [music] was that poor old Picasso he'd fallen off in those years. Here was this old man obsessed with [music] girls and sex and near pornographic subjects sometimes. What we've tried to do, I think, in this exhibition is to show that [music] he didn't fall off. It's a different Picasso. Maybe it's not quite as great a Picasso as the Cubist Picasso [music] or Surrealist Picasso, but he's this extraordinary protean figure, painter, sculptor, [music] draftsman, printmaker. &gt;&gt; I think late Picasso is more a medical case than an art historical or critical [music] case. Well, it's simply an old man not able to paint anymore. He's able to paint, but he's using paint as a for therapeutic [music] purposes. The pictures are full of tricks and mannerisms. They're dependent entirely on references to other people's paintings and to his own earlier pictures. &gt;&gt; In her biography, Picasso's granddaughter Marina stated, \"No one in my family was able to escape the stranglehold of his genius.\" He wrote hundreds of poems throughout his life, often incorporating surrealist and experimental techniques. Some of his poems were even published in literary journals and anthologies. Following the death of Picasso's mother, Maria, in 1938, his attention was shattered thanks [music] to the incoming threat of the Second World War. &gt;&gt; Picasso's decision to stay in Paris during this tumultuous period was a source of controversy and debate. Being an outspoken artist who promoted liberty, he was under surveillance from the Nazis. Though he was being watched, the artist continued to resist [music] alongside his fellow Parisians, signing partitions against fascism and oppression, and taking part in secret resistance gatherings who were opposed to the Nazi atrocities. During World War II, &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Picasso's famous anti-war masterpiece Guernica was kept hidden in a Parisian apartment to protect it from being confiscated or destroyed by the Nazis. The painting was eventually unveiled to the public after the war ended. &gt;&gt; Probably the most famous image in 20th century [music] art, Picasso's Guernica, last shown at the Whitechapel Art Gallery","t0":2200,"t1":2400,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"15":0.04169374036984264,"1938":0.061716412053348386,"know":0.03497017959482788,"last":0.06614089009151361,"great":0.050170557179229434,"picassos":0.05309311672926254,"private":0.043004507934793934,"hands":0.0444698214051767,"terms":0.05031703569392849,"picasso":0.31330062145799736,"quality":0.05031703569392849,"absolutely":0.056672107656114065,"top":0.0444698214051767,"end":0.08101601375288901,"therefore":0.04613105680500552,"naturally":0.061716412053348386,"enormously":0.061716412053348386,"important":0.06376942310471732,"uh":0.02413995422746438,"culmination":0.056672107656114065,"series":0.048048812332028235,"paintings":0.06741714782740112,"he":0.1511438148402931,"large":0.048048812332028235,"painting":0.06058872802084551,"well":0.04334213737267382,"dimensions":0.06171641