 depression. And if you do this for long enough, it leads to burnout. Has anybody ever felt burnout on creating content? I mean, everybody's hand should be up right now. Let's tell the truth, people, please. Okay? And then what happens is eventually burnout leads to you quitting. So I presented to you a very structured argument why neither option is good. Yes, maybe we can argue later. So the problem with virality is it's based on an outcome. Do I get to go viral or not? And we have to ask this question. Is there something beneath the surface that's a bigger problem? So I'm going to present to you four really quick problems and we'll go through this. Okay. Number one is the seduction. Okay. Virality feels a lot of times very opaque. None of the platforms tell you how to go viral. So there's all these professional gurus, coaches, and programs that you can enter telling you what they guess what it is even","t0":800,"t1":1000,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"10":0.03219168293487686,"100":0.04902021886337028,"confidence":0.04902021886337028,"yes":0.06899325016682521,"like":0.01648845849526139,"know":0.018580171105508046,"mean":0.09819404234352122,"okay":0.19077043928078116,"happens":0.1195705542564289,"now":0.1474634785391113,"well":0.023028315490316212,"loop":0.13116335223383876,"went":0.040836554717706766,"viral":0.40836554717706763,"need":0.05785641267735357,"go":0.17956278157875427,"again":0.1432788915117504,"there":0.05144878047956532,"little":0.02737112111244338,"problem":0.1491604785244612,"here":0.054017816373837624,"then":0.04943653120290794,"enter":0.13116335223383876,"trap":0.06022144978152234,"called":0.032731347447840405,"validation":0.06022144978152234,"where":0.023028315490316212,"re":0.03792676948398801,"looking":0.06776326609202925,"outside":0.04902021886337028,"validated":0.13116335223383876,"versus":0.08609000098115054,"inwards":0.06022144978152234,"right":0.06677401122930773,"exttrinsic":0.06558167611691938,"intrinsic":0.06558167611691938,"even":0.0488