 me. Like, I'm I'm up for an award. Please vote for me. Please nominate me as a speaker for this event. or who knows an organizer who can put me in touch with somebody who will do the introductions. So, you can test the strength of those relationships in the community just to see how sticky it is. Okay, now here's the story. I'm sure some of you know this. VidCon is a big conference for YouTubers to create content. Post pandemic, they open it back up in 2022. Tik Tok is blowing up like crazy. It's sweeping all over social media. There's a good chance that if you're on Tik Tok, it's because it was in 2022 that everybody was telling you you must be on Tik Tok. Yes. Okay. So, what did VidCon do? They invited some of the biggest Tik Tockers with millions of followers to come and speak. I was at that conference. And this is an illustration of what those rooms looked like. Massive rooms for 500 to 800 people. Even for some of the biggest creators that you know and love, about 20 to 30 seats. Not percentage, 20 to 30 seats. fewer people than the people in this room for a room six times as big as this room. So, there was a Business Insider article in July of 2022. Why Tik Tockers may face problems forming deep connections with fans despite the platform's hold on Gen Z. And there's a woman, her name is Grace Africa. She has 1.3 million followers on Tik Tok. She she said, \"When you set up a meet and greet and no one comes, how heartbreaking is that? this relationship that you thought you were building wasn't a relationship at all because you're","t0":1600,"t1":1800,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"20":0.07125510980764689,"30":0.0846593513843254,"500":0.04683467246092962,"800":0.06265774391859816,"2022":0.18797323175579447,"viral":0.03901587363302792,"doesn":0.10072455970836115,"mean":0.06254406742642986,"ve":0.05527690818885772,"done":0.03901587363302792,"anything":0.03720843285490645,"valuable":0.0846593513843254,"sure":0.08005371233851451,"scrolled":0.06265774391859816,"thro