":0.07519371166792543}},{"id":"doc_1785765215478_14t4u0_c12","text":"I did it for 15 years. So, if you want to criticize me for pursuing the money, you do something for 15 years where you don't get paid and tell me how you like it. On the other side, I was running my production company, making commercials and music videos for uh what Caitlyn was sharing with you all. I won't repeat that now. I made a lot of money. I made millions of dollars. Actually, I made a couple million dollars before I turned 25. But the corporate overlords always told me what to do. Oh, make it bigger. Oh, uh, that pixel, can you move it one pixel to the left? We don't like that shade of green. Can you make it more emerald? Oh, okay. Right. So, when my friend invited me to make YouTube content with him, I finally found something where I could merge all of the things that I love. Entrepreneurship. I love reading. I love teaching. I love drawing. I like comic books. I I consume pop culture, art, history, design, literature, everything. I get to combine everything about me and I get to put it out into the world and I'll figure out a way to make money. So, the first part, there's a reason why no circle exists on here that says make money. Because I believe when you find that sweet spot in the middle of all these things, the money comes. I suggest to you right now, if the money hasn't come, it's because one of these circles is missing or it's not complete. And I encourage you to investigate that. Okay, I have a story to share with you. Her name is Simona and she was my driver from Black Lane and she took me from my house to the airport in Los Angeles and Simona was this incredible Middle Eastern woman and I happened to be sitting in the front seat. I was just talking to her and she's super interesting. I'm like, \"Hey, uh, what are your passions in life? What do you do?\" She goes, \"Well, I drive for work.\" I I'll put it here. I drive for work. My passion is I'm a hair stylist. I I love to do co