6274254629,"person":0.05670132917967449,"life":0.02403614138344568,"workshops":0.053894016008763056,"concepts":0.051464547251475895,"help":0.04465770051769266,"figure":0.07084277005324453,"themselves":0.07850960462117314,"were":0.07855520860665559,"meant":0.047631129967511586,"lifetime":0.04941046068518941,"thought":0.0751739601618153,"old":0.030937829703048605,"grow":0.04941046068518941,"happened":0.04465770051769266,"plan":0.06070086274254629,"always":0.0628448706923866,"making":0.03299191626933509,"book":0.06711806214235334,"versus":0.04338767459120437,"sales":0.041161647748284035,"together":0.03610487774335963,"realized":0.046061649044369796,"ability":0.046061649044369796,"teach":0.041161647748284035,"finite":0.06070086274254629,"experience":0.04338767459120437,"through":0.09141069396030119,"price":0.047631129967511586,"barrier":0.0661037609496524,"fundamental":0.06070086274254629,"overall":0.06070086274254629,"well":0.023211640085732933,"being":0.027964400253229674,"sense":0.03839481447644119,"able":0.03542138502662227,"standalone":0.0661037609496524,"thing":0.022947766382731147,"done":0.041161647748284035,"own":0.055178036124457985,"pace":0.056867445458582,"privacy":0.06070086274254629,"comfort":0.0661037609496524,"home":0.03925480231058657,"ask":0.040174145194119,"deeply":0.06070086274254629,"personal":0.03610487774335963,"profound":0.06070086274254629,"questions":0.04465770051769266,"require":0.056867445458582,"really":0.022435196014621704,"kind":0.0314224353461933,"contemplative":0.0661037609496524,"reflective":0.06070086274254629,"moment":0.041161647748284035,"conducive":0.0661037609496524,"around":0.029581556313292675}},{"id":"doc_1785765215770_m53hnx_c1","text":"timetable. So, I recommend people go through the book at a certain pace that they feel comfortable with. And, the goal is not to try to finish it as quickly as possible, but to learn about things that you kind of buried way deep inside of you and to have some honest conversations with yourself. &gt;&gt; Mhm. When did you start to unblend yourself? &gt;&gt; It's been a progression of exploring is it safe? I'm going to be okay. I think for me doing video with Jose in was how I was able to do this at scale. So, prior to that point in time, it's not like I was sitting here trying to fit in. I've always been intrigued by this idea of pushing buttons and using the things I say, my actions, and the way that I dress to kind of push people's buttons. And, this has happened, but now it's happening at a much larger scale. So, it's kind of that that expression of you can't put the genie back in the bottle. So, you do it in measured steps. Like, if I showed up and dressed like this and said these things, what what is the consequence of that? And, like like many things, there's a quote. The quote is something like the human mind once expanded does not shrink back to its original size. And, this is like many things. When you find out that these self-imposed rules that you live by are actually just that, self-imposed and not real rules, they're not laws, that you start to be more free. &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; It's it's this classic story of a dog who who wears electric shock collar and when they approach the perimeter to a fence that they're not supposed to go beyond, it sends them a little electric signal. After a while they learn that there's a perimeter and you can just take it off and they never cross that boundary. And the same as about elephant who's one since childbirth is is held by chain and then eventually it's just a string and they never push past. We are like that. We learn really fast about what we can and cannot do according to certain societal norms and then we place small for the rest of our lives and we never realize that once we leave the city where in which we we grew up in or we leave the group of friends that we thought this is my core group I must need them always or the job that we've always had. We learn that the world's much bigger. There's a lot more to us to give and I think that's one of the most liberating things. &gt;&gt; With Jose, I guess what was that chain that you had to let go? Like what was holding on to you? &gt;&gt; I think the biggest hurdle I had to get through was if I am myself what kind of negative impact is","t0":200,"t1":400,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"timetable":0.07960769102764781,"recommend":0.06490369251353882,"people":0.04651368789063403,"go":0.09341401842513378,"through":0.07338961431616592,"book":0.0404145987810927,"certain":0.11472280013354785,"pace":0.06848454554721087,"feel":0.03322500859409376,"comfortable":0.06848454554721087,"goal":0.050854777070652314,"try":0.045265392678977105,"finish":0.06197792255108925,"quickly":0.05736140006677393,"possible":0.05378054703310189,"learn":0.1890956961479211,"things":0.17165091665867066,"kind":0.15136612431363633,"buried":0.07960769102764781,"way":0.0546480324414809,"deep":0.05378054703310189,"inside":0.05547129955496763,"some":0.02701834399160781,"honest":0.07310106803152618,"conversations":0.06848454554721087,"yourself":0.07338961431616592,"gt":0.3068599401317523,"mhm":0.09676214762876074,"start":0.07124918041801524,"unblend":0.06848454554721087,"progression":0.07960769102764781,"exploring":0.05736140006677393,"safe":0.06848454554721087,"going":0.02701834399160781,"okay":0.028946336626861233,"think":0.07589202618165546,"me":0.025297342060551817,"doing":0.03414224719854017,"video":0.044348154074530695,"jose":0.12980738502707764,"able":0.04265740155266496,"scale":0.12980738502707764,"prior":0.07310106803152618,"point":0.047273924036980275,"time":0.02642393133981274,"like":0.18013374595146886,"sitting":0.05378054703310189,"here":0.032785328848642104,"trying":0.03907654851899292,"fit":0.07310106803152618,"ve":0.07023021821180013,"always":0.11352459323522725,"intrigued":0.07960769102764781,"idea":0.044348154074530695,"pushing":0.06490369251353882,"buttons":0.14620213606305235,"say":0.02732401622074045,"actions":0.07960769102764781,"dress":0.06197792255108925,"push":0.13696909109442174,"happened":0.05378054703310189,"now":0.02557166167764602,"happening":0.06490369251353882,"much":0.07451585666788689,"larger":0.07310106803152618,"expression":0.052251075334358646,"put":0.035115109105900065,"genie":0.07960769102764781,"back":0.06828449439708034,"bottle":0.06848454554721087,"measured":0.06848454554721087,"steps":0.07960769102764781,"showed":0.06848454554721087,"dressed":0.06490369251353882,"said":0.03037370422616586,"consequence":0.06848454554721087,"many":0.060009568746969555,"there":0.06245217967385651,"quote":0.08869630814906139,"something":0.024762382296113532,"human":0.045265392678977105,"mind":0.047273924036980275,"once":0.08225585970784342,"expanded":0.07310106803152618,"shrink":0.07310106803152618,"original":0.05950421929481731,"size":0.06197792255108925,"find":0.046238254586337,"self":0.09454784807396055,"imposed":0.14620213606305235,"rules":0.10450215066871729,"live":0.04957030718161432,"actually":0.04187445081825876,"just":0.059461036409072826,"real":0.03844716170117739,"re":0.046038203436206473,"laws":0.07310106803152618,"free":0.05378054703310189,"classic":0.06490369251353882,"story":0.03973163159021538,"dog":0.07310106803152618,"wears":0.07960769102764781,"electric":0.13696909109442174,"shock":0.06490369251353882,"collar":0.07960769102764781,"approach":0.05950421929481731,"perimeter":0.15921538205529562,"fence":0.07960769102764781,"supposed":0.06490369251353882,"beyond":0.05736140006677393,"sends":0.07960769102764781,"little":0.03322500859409376,"signal":0.07960769102764781,"after":0.03973163159021538,"while":0.047273924036980275,"take":0.03562459020900762,"off":0.0404145987810927,"never":0.09460276821668408,"cross":0.07310106803152618,"boundary":0.07960769102764781,"same":0.03784153107840908,"elephant":0.07310106803152618,"since":0.06490369251353882,"childbirth":0.07960769102764781,"held":0.06197792255108925,"chain":0.14620213606305235,"then":0.060009568746969555,"eventually":0.04957030718161432,"string":0.07960769102764781,"past":0.05547129955496763,"really":0.02701834399160781,"fast":0.05736140006677393,"cannot":0.06197792255108925,"according":0.07960769102764781,"societal":0.07960769102764781,"norms":0.06848454554721087,"place":0.05378054703310189,"small":0.050854777070652314,"rest":0.06490369251353882,"lives":0.06848454554721087,"realize":0.05736140006677393,"leave":0.10756109406620377,"city":0.052251075334358646,"where":0.027953403038555983,"grew":0.05736140006677393,"group":0.1239558451021785,"friends":0.047273924036980275,"thought":0.045265392678977105,"core":0.06197792255108925,"must":0.052251075334358646,"need":0.035115109105900065,"job":0.050854777070652314,"had":0.08197204866222135,"world":0.025850752309142456,"bigger":0.05736140006677393,"lot":0.03153425607222802,"us":0.032785328848642104,"give":0.03784153107840908,"most":0.028608486109778442,"liberating":0.07960769102764781,"guess":0.05950421929481731,"let":0.031138006141711257,"holding":0.07960769102764781,"biggest":0.06490369251353882,"hurdle":0.07960769102764781,"am":0.052251075334358646,"myself":0.050854777070652314,"negative":0.06490369251353882,"impact":0.04838107381438037}},{"id":"doc_1785765215770_m53hnx_c2","text":"it going to have on my business? Cuz at that point in time I'm still running a service design company doing really big projects and if I say this, does it mean that I lose that? And that was the thing I need to figure out. So a couple things to learn in that process. And number one, nobody's really paying attention to you. In our own little bubble, I think we we falsely believe we're the most important thing in the world because we have no other thing to reference. We're always thinking about ourselves. We're looking at ourselves. We're just dealing with ourselves most of the time. And we don't realize clients are busy. They're thinking about themselves. So they're not sitting there looking at every social post that you make and just listening to every podcast like, oh my god, we disagree politically. We can no longer work with that person. Unless you do something super sensational in a in a way that's not good for you. And and number two is there's a wider level of acceptance for you than you think. So even if they were paying attention what do I inevitably happen is as you show more of yourself, some people get to say I like that guy or I like her or I don't like that person. And I think that's a good thing. People are so afraid of alienating everyone that they wind up saying nothing to everyone and and they're just blinding themselves to into oblivion, into irrelevancy. So, when you say something and you say something that is based on your convictions, not to say it's to rile people up. I'm not saying to be a contrarian, to be divisive, but to say things that have meaning to you. It should both compel and repel. It should compel people to say, \"Yo, I get your vibe. I get what you're putting down. I want to be around you. This is cool. Let's chop it up sometime.\" And it should repel the people who are like, \"I don't like the way you think. I don't like that expression of whatever.\" For example, sometimes I wear fashion that is unpalatable for some people. Uh if I wear some kind of weird skirt short thing, they're like, \"Well, I don't I don't like that. I don't get that.\" Or some crazy color or floral print. For some people some straight people they might think that shoe's nasty. Like, \"You can't do that.\" Or if I talk about therapy and how that's been one of the biggest return on investments I've ever had, they're like, \"Well, don't bring your therapy agenda to this conversation. Everybody needs it.\" I never said everybody needs it, but if you're searching and you're lost, it's worked really well for me. I recommend you give it a try. That's all it is. I'm not trying to impose anything on anybody. For the people who feel called, try it. If","t0":400,"t1":600,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"going":0.02727295329829548,"bu