one has an a-hole and everyone has an opinion. That doesn't mean I want to see either. Let's just put that out into the universe, okay? And everybody needs to know that. And sometimes they both stink. Now, getting into it. So, I used to not dress as maybe as progressively as I do today. And just the act of wearing a hat bothers people. Like, \"Oh, no one would take themselves seriously. If you walked into me, I would never hire you.\" Bro, trust me, you don't have enough money to hire me. So, let's start there. You probably have never hired anybody. And these kinds of ideas about asking people to meet you where you are to be able to have the pleasure of your company is ridiculous. We all come in different shapes, sizes, and have different preferences about how we carry ourselves. To each their own. Especially in this country about self-expression and freedom, your First Amendment right. We should accept people for who they are. Or we should just decide this is not for me, and that's totally okay. But to project your your values and your aesthetic onto people is just ridiculous to me. Nobody asked you. Nobody cares. So, people would say things like, \"Your hat.\" Or \"Who do you think he is? He's trying too hard.\" Or \"Every time I tune in, there's another necklace, and it's just getting out of control.\" &gt;&gt; Don't forget the skirts. &gt;&gt; Well, well, they're not even there yet cuz I","t0":600,"t1":800,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"50":0.05287945088563583,"worries":0.0733875216245594,"find":0.04262541551617406,"whoever":0.06738929545235584,"think":0.06996218129983907,"most":0.026373153974508727,"aligned":0.05983242418369914,"way":0.05037809300543535,"want":0.09852294799825366,"learn":0.04358016264203382,"gt":0.37717780282157015,"interesting":0.05287945088563583,"because":0.023072091903110267,"guys":0.04569711724164123,"know":0.04158334429765217,"work":0.022587017430595328,"behind":0.051137033910690514,"scenes":0.06313348625509761,"future":0.0571352600828940