. And if we have high self-awareness, we're not quite sure what's interesting to other people. Historically speaking, we are the worst judge of our own value. I could do something, you're like, \"Dude, how did you do that? Why did you even move that there or put that thing on? How did you know that's going to work?\" And I'm like, \"Well, doesn't everybody know that?\" Yeah, well, I don't, explain it to me. And then I would explain it to you and depending on your reaction to me explaining it to you, I could think, \"Maybe I'm on to something. Maybe somebody else like you would want to know this thing. And that begins the process of understanding, \"Wow, something I take for granted is valuable to other people.\" So, if we want to learn more about ourselves, we need to put ourselves in a position where we're explaining to people what it is that we know, think, and believe. And judging by their reaction, and if you get enough feedback from different types of people, you might discover something you weren't even aware about yourself. &gt;&gt; You're so aligned with who you are, so I think it's easy for you to talk about these things cuz you're already and you do all these different things. But I think for like a lot of us, me being video production, and build my business for past 10 years around video production. When I like, \"Hey Chris, how do I make this video about that?\" You're like, \"No, that's boring. Talk about this other thing.\" And I'm just and I just I don't see it like the way that you do. For me, it's so easy like, \"Well, I can build a","t0":1200,"t1":1400,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"10":0.03840245431066686,"locks":0.0782344099807338,"behind":0.05451438592836754,"never":0.03099027099197386,"leave":0.10570559982991007,"there":0.04091656108200283,"only":0.07556784959585969,"path":0.05847773535194543,"forward":0.05637188105775263,"re":0.15835405757514032,"door":0.3365157275962161,"go":0.03060085661355508,"locked":0.0782344099807338,"want":0.07877243162