 building a personal brand.\" But I think for you, you're so aligned that like when you hear when you say this to me, yeah, it makes sense for you, but like I don't feel like it'd work for me. &gt;&gt; What wouldn't work for you? &gt;&gt; Like to not talk about videos. Like I don't know how to not build a personal brand around the thing that I've been doing for 10 years. &gt;&gt; Okay, let's clarify. Talking about what you do is not how you build a personal brand. You're basically doing tutorials. Nobody has any sense of who you are, what you stand for. Uh your the all the things you've learned in life is just manifested in how to. &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; So, if we said this, if we put a robot voice on you, but it's the exact same script, and we blur your face, would anybody be able to tell it's you? &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; Cuz you're not really sharing your philosophy and your ways to the world. Now, let's let's uh contrast that against some some people who have very strong personal brands, but maybe not put a lot of value into the world. Uh we were talking to Manager John earlier today. He's like, \"In the OG days, all you had to do is turn on the camera and be a personality.\" So, we got to know those people really well, and they grew gigantic accounts and have massive fandoms. But to the average person, it's like, \"What value did you give to me?\" So, the blend is Or, I'm sorry, the solution is somewhere in between the two to say like, I create a lot of value in the world. I give you a lot of utility. I'm useful. I'm helpful to you creating transformation. But, I'm also weaving in my story about who I am. So, you have a choice. Do I want your brand of video production or do I want someone else's brand of video production? The classic example I always give to, and I'm sorry if people are bored out of this until you they can understand this concept. Water's water. Water's two two uh what is it? Two molecules of hydrogen and one molecule of oxygen or something like 