es the top 100 films of all time great? And then you could do that research and you can start thinking about it. And then you can maybe come up with a couple of things that are obvious between these things and a couple things that are not obvious that you start to share with the world. You could do this in intimate conversation with you and another person off camera. You could do this in small workshops, virtual workshops. And then you start to see what ideas stick. Now you have something. And when you go and make content around that, something you thought about, that's going to hit much harder. Can we see the difference between these two approaches? &gt;&gt; I want to say no, because that to me feels like what you just said of like you're a how-to person. Like if you're coming if you're like looking at these books like, \"Hey, here are five books for you to go read.\" How's that different than what you said to that like to be a how-to person? &gt;&gt; Okay, these these are two different arguments we're making. I asked you, can you see the difference between someone who wings it, who doesn't do any research, and one person who does a deep dive and try to like fill in the knowledge gaps that they may or may not may not have. &gt;&gt; Okay. &gt;&gt; Which one will be more valuable? &gt;&gt; The second one. &gt;&gt; The second one. The problem is most people don't go this path as you know. &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; So, when you say, \"I don't know how","t0":1800,"t1":2000,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"100":0.0506651100017633,"us":0.05583040370063679,"paralyzed":0.06778229293151075,"even":0.05048127410719475,"just":0.05062834175772335,"doing":0.02907055550886114,"work":0.06258556487690671,"book":0.03441117482402686,"like":0.1704173467177562,"some":0.046009758185988577,"make":0.1428062335736333,"post":0.08897878203928562,"then":0.10219078370425409,"say":0.11632572479060786,"hey":0.08660101434602512,"got":0.03382965962622291,"deep":0.09158333186044963,"before":0.05172362847