ndational layer or something like that. And there are these three things. The cool thing is you only need to know one of these things to figure out the other two. So what I want you to imagine is either a triangle or three overlapping circles, the Venn diagram. Okay? Where they meet in the middle is where you are in your personal brand. And they are what is the one thing you want to be known for? And I'd like to reduce it down to a word if possible. There's some conditions there. So first, what's the one thing you want to be known for? Number two, who's the enemy? What are you on a mission to rid the world of? What do you want to eradicate? And this, there are only so many versions of this, right? So it's universal. There's probably 12 universal concepts, I just made up the number, that everybody's trying to get rid of, like hate, poverty, whatever else that they're trying to get rid of the world of, right? Judgment, let's say. And then the last one is and it's the bridge between these two things, your your one thing, the enemy, the the thing that you're trying to eradicate the world of, and your call to arms or your rallying cry, the phrase that when you say activates your audience and the community. And so, do you know the one thing you want to be known for, Rodrigo? Or of these three things, what do you think you're clearest about? &gt;&gt; The one thing I want to be known for. &gt;&gt; Which is? &gt;&gt; A YouTube strategist. &gt;&gt; As a YouTube strategist, okay. &gt;&gt; That's what I want to work on for 2026. &gt;&gt; Perfect. YouTube","t0":2200,"t1":2400,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"12":0.05221234090572293,"30":0.0537406787864158,"100":0.05946010801249345,"2026":0.06193197747909441,"he":0.021646124898778454,"said":0.030351187788538073,"find":0.046203977543021545,"effective":0.07954867676990798,"there":0.14561372706683623,"high":0.04834520827019797,"frequency":0.07304687722138986,"exercises":0.15909735353981597,"low":0.05946010801249345,"intellectual":0.07