":0.05946010801249345}},{"id":"doc_1785765215770_m53hnx_c12","text":"strategist. The The criteria now we have to ask ourselves this question. Can you own this space? Because the world rewards number one, not number two, three, or four. If you cannot own this space within a relatively short amount of time, and when I say short, between one to two years, then you should not try. Something from Seth Godin's book The Dip is we should predetermine if we're going to be successful, and once we determine we can be successful, we never quit. What people do is they don't think, they try things and they quit, they think and they try things and they quit, they never get anywhere. So, if you look up right now on the internet, type onto Google or Gemini or anything and say, \"Who are the world's most for for foremost thought leaders in the in the YouTube strategy space?\" Get a list, double-check your homework, and say to yourself, \"Can I with intentional effort overtake them in a year's time?\" If you think you realistically can, I would suggest you go for it. &gt;&gt; I understand &gt;&gt; What do you mean? &gt;&gt; one thing, right? But why do I need an enemy? Like, if I'm just trying to be the like the YouTube strategist, why do I need an enemy for that? &gt;&gt; rid of something in the world. &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; Because we are more united in a common enemy than we are in a common friend. And all the best brands in the world, as far as I know, they have an enemy. And we can go through this exercise if you we say like here's a clear clear brand, and what are they trying to get rid of in the world? If we can't identify that, there's a big part of the triangle that's missing. &gt;&gt; Can you give me an example? &gt;&gt; Yeah, pick a brand. We'll try this live and freestyle. &gt;&gt; One of your favorites. &gt;&gt; Who? &gt;&gt; Louis Vuitton. &gt;&gt; Louis Vuitton. Okay, Louis Vuitton is a brand. What is the one thing they want to be known for? &gt;&gt; You're asking me that question? &gt;&gt; Yeah. &gt;&gt; Oh, luxury goods. &gt;&gt; They're trunks company, by the way. &gt;&gt; That's what they're known for, being a trunk company. &gt;&gt; literally what they say all the time. We're not a fashion company, we're trunks company. We make trunks. And trunks are bags, they're interchangeable those words. &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; That's what they're known for. &gt;&gt; Okay. &gt;&gt; And you know why they say that? &gt;&gt; Why? &gt;&gt; Cuz that's what they sell the most of. &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; So, let's Okay, side detour here. Why did they appoint Pharrell Williams, who's not a designer, to run one of the most uh profitable largest fashion houses in the world, LVMH group, right? &gt;&gt; Right. &gt;&gt; Why? &gt;&gt; For clout. &gt;&gt; Well, he's been designing fashion that has a lot of mixed reviews. I love Louis Vuitton as","t0":2400,"t1":2600,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"strategist":0.06529078860146217,"criteria":0.03850424621326388,"now":0.026938527270045694,"ask":0.025483578125118447,"ourselves":0.030213751054308402,"question":0.04980082670753886,"own":0.035000963619110766,"space":0.08035962716459487,"because":0.02636541905740768,"world":0.0816976078609455,"rewards":0.0360726029668412,"number":0.04332631464848888,"four":0.027522009236777237,"cannot":0.03264539430073109,"within":0.030213751054308402,"relatively":0.03418647393241234,"short":0.05221995694412707,"amount":0.02832762201987954,"time":0.04175452913184836,"say":0.08635364788198766,"between":0.02490041335376943,"years":0.017268890977441213,"then":0.01580430541171165,"try":0.09536986922816203,"something":0.026085989997993633,"seth":0.03850424621326388,"godin":0.03850424621326388,"book":0.021287427174201564,"dip":0.041931454879374,"predetermine":0.041931454879374,"re":0.09699810785579935,"going":0.014231269081853475,"successful":0.06529078860146217,"once":0.02166315732424444,"determine":0.041931454879374,"never":0.03321983638962791,"quit":0.09402729011295372,"people":0.012