n find a niche within YouTube that I could be that strategist for. &gt;&gt; Possibly. &gt;&gt; Okay. &gt;&gt; It only takes one dimension for you to then change the game. So one level of specificity will will change it for you. &gt;&gt; Right. &gt;&gt; I want to be the YouTube strategist for Latin America. Boom. You can own that. &gt;&gt; Okay. &gt;&gt; Only adding one more dimension. &gt;&gt; Okay. &gt;&gt; it takes. And and I want to tell you something. You're like, \"It's discouraging.\" I don't see it as discouraging at all. Because if you're number one, it means you're number one and nobody can take it away from you. You see? The the coin has two sides. You only look at the side of like, \"Well, that doesn't That's not cool.\" But the good side to the coin is once you own it, it's kind of hard to undo it. Because the human brain works like this. Once something occupies a space in your mind, it's very hard for you to undo that. And not to get political, but Trump is great at doing this. When he calls Hillary Clinton \"Crooked Hillary\", we can't stop thinking \"What? Is she Is she crooked?\" Like you have to double-check yourself, cuz he made the name stick. &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; Right? This is the power of words. When it's associated with something, it's very hard for us to uncouple it. So, what you need to do is think \"What do I want to be associated with?\" And kind of own it. And if I can't, I'm going to work like a dog to own it. &gt;&gt; So, is your book teaching you how to find this one thing for you to be known for, or is that there's are there different elements to the personal branding and what you call it? &gt;&gt; than that. There's seven points, but I realized in trying to make it simpler, is it simple enough? So, I've done this a couple of","t0":3200,"t1":3400,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"right":0.073613350985336,"um":0.02961642318471843,"familiar":0.044208652265359846,"writer":0.054224168055698185,"named":0.03663220704941055,"ryan":0.054224168