 that we had to like solve some of our own problems because when they took Accelerator with them, they also took a large chunk of revenue away from us and we had to see, can we still do this? Are we still relevant? What are we all about? So, last year was about this idea of like getting really super hyper focused and executing on ideas that we talked about, but we never execute. So, the smaller your team the more work you have to do. Everybody understands that. But, the smaller your team, the less friction there is to do what it is that you want to do. You don't have so many different opinions about what we should and shouldn't do, and then therefore you can just execute on those things. And there's one big thing that's happened last year that that is materialized this year, which is we need office space. And in order for me to acquire more office space I have to get the financials in the company back on track. So, for the past couple years I've been on semi-retirement mode. I work for fun. It's a lifestyle business. As long as we don't lose money, I'm okay. So, my wife comes to me and says, \"I just you know, I have to pull money from our other money-making things to support just our current bills.\" I'm like, \"Okay. How much more money do I need to make?\" She goes, \"Well, $20,000 more a month would probably do it. That's how much short we are.\" I said, \"I can do that.\" And then now I want to acquire property, which means that number's even high and much higher. So, the goal posts just moved, right? So, if I want to maintain our lifestyle, I needed to earn $20,000 more a month so that she's not withdrawing money from other accounts. But, now if I want to acquire a property, I've got to do in orders of magnitude more than that.","t0":4200,"t1":4400,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"20":0.08806603078023655,"2025":0.0774403242020303,"2026":0.1205810733552811,"cuz":0.036243559033442334,"think":0.024608606848531958,"re":0.04478478591397223,"person":0.0332127041735521