y unknown artist to becoming an absolute superstar that same year in October of 1982 Bishop Berger would\n  - [≈13:54] to work together frequently and created famous works such as Armen Hammer 2 and Untitled General Electric too it made for a timely combination as Warhol in the early 80s was struggling\n  - [≈14:54] and the relationship never recovered from there on February 22nd 1987 Andy warhall passed away his heart stopped beating after he had been recovering from gallbladder surgery basad struggled to cope with\n  - [≈15:29] 12th 1988 from a heroin overdose he was found unresponsive in his home by his girlfriend Kelly imman the greatest black contemporary artist of his generation was Gone Too Soon at the\n  QUOTE: \"and the relationship never recovered from there on February 22nd 1987 Andy warhall passed away his heart stopped beating after he had been recovering from gallbladder surgery basad struggled to cope with\" (≈14:54)\n[16:00–16:53] Only · National · Recognition\n  - [≈16:03] but the fact is that he has created enough work to Intrigue generations to come only now will people begin to understand the magnitude of his contribution bosia left the world with\n  - [≈16:16] over a thousand paintings and drawings after his death the New York Times indicated that bosia was the most famous of only a small number of young black artists who have achieved\n  - [≈16:29] National recognition his stamp on pop culture is unparalleled from references by musicians to his influence and fashion Basia was able to leave his mark in the world contributing the best way\n  - [≈16:42] he knew how from rebellious Street kid to a legend in the art World a leader in the neoexpressionism movement Jean Michelle's work will continue to reverberate Through Time\n  QUOTE: \"National recognition his stamp on pop culture is unparalleled from references by musicians to his influence and fashion Basia was able to leave his mark in the world contributing the best way\" (≈16:29)\n\nTAKEAWAYS 