ca itself, the Basque town obliterated by German bombers in the Spanish Civil War.\"\n\nQUESTIONS THIS ANSWERS:\n  - What does the source teach about gt?\n  - What does the source teach about music?\n  - What does the source teach about his?\n  - What does the source teach about picasso?\n  - How does picasso untold story apply today?","uploadedAt":"2026-08-22T14:54:38.461Z","kind":"digest","title":"He's a very special figure, a genius unequivocally. [music] &gt;&gt; When we sat in","source":"picasso_untold_story","durationSec":2748,"tsMode":"duration","chunks":[{"id":"doc_1787410478461_jpjk55_c0","text":"DIGEST · TURTLE · picasso_untold_story · runtime ≈45:48 · mode:estimate TITLE: He's a very special figure, a genius unequivocally. [music] &gt;&gt; When we sat in THESIS: &gt;&gt; Just off 5th Avenue, on a site long occupied by the old-fashioned town dwellings of the Rockefeller family, stands the spanking new home of a nationally important institution, the New York Museum of Modern Art. CHAPTERS: [0:00–5:20] Young · Pepe · Fine - [≈0:52] &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Pablo Picasso was born on the 25th [music] of October to father Don Jose Ruiz Blasco, nicknamed Pepe, and his mother [music] Maria Picasso y Lopez. - [≈1:41] He began by drawing animals such as donkeys [music] and dogs, completing the images with a single line, beginning at the head and ending at the tail. - [≈2:35] In 1892, Picasso [music] began studying at the School of Fine Arts in La Coruña, where his father Don José taught. - [≈4:45] In 1899, Picasso attended [music] a cafe named Els Quatre Gats to meet a circle of avant-garde artists. QUOTE: \"In 1892, Picasso [music] began studying at the School of Fine Arts in La Coruña, where his father Don José taught.\" (≈2:35) [5:20–10:40] Carles · Guitarist · Blue - [≈5:25] The two settled in a vacant studio whilst attending exhibitions such as the Universal, which raked in over 32 million visitors, all pining to see [music] the next influx of creative talent