0.05042373056234439,"motifs":0.05042373056234439,"inspired":0.03260865637746091,"iberian":0.04723934089263768,"sculptures":0.03956680606086989,"observed":0.05042373056234439,"louvre":0.05042373056234439,"said":0.020951205219327536,"me":0.017449626857087876,"picture":0.041044882131551545,"well":0.019281727354638473,"knew":0.03709680153952196}},{"id":"doc_1787410478461_jpjk55_c1","text":"was bought that there was something on the &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; back, but we didn't know how important, how brilliant a picture it was until we removed the backing of the frame and saw that it was picture painted in oil 4 y… - [≈17:52] &gt;&gt; Just off 5th Avenue, on a site long occupied by the old-fashioned town dwellings of the Rockefeller family, stands the spanking new home of a nationally important institution, the New York Museum of Modern Art. - [≈18:32] &gt;&gt; Well, I think we went started initially in in the '50s, '54, something like this, but in 1963, uh &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; we went as usual during the summer holidays with the children, and so on. - [≈19:36] And he took [music] something out of his white coat, which was a little medallion like this, and with a with a ribbon, he pinned it round Sheila's neck, [music] and said that he much preferred to give presents to women than he did to men. QUOTE: \"&gt;&gt; Just off 5th Avenue, on a site long occupied by the old-fashioned town dwellings of the Rockefeller family, stands the spanking new home of a nationally important institution, the New York Museum of Modern Art.\" (≈17:52) [21:20–26:40] Humor · Jacqueline · Last - [≈22:46] &gt;&gt; Picasso bought his first painting in 1908, a portrait of a woman made in 1895 by French artist [music] Henri Rousseau. - [≈23:39] Recent art frauds and record-breaking high prices for master works have kept all kinds of art in the world news spotlight. - [≈23:56] In 1909, the two temporarily [music] settled in a Paris studio, and together they visited Horta, a neighborhood in Barcelona. - [≈25:30] It's very much a a paean to uh to Jacqueline, um his last uh and and longest-lasting muse of his life, um who he would marry about 5 years after this picture was painted. QUOTE: \"It's very much a a paean to uh to Jacqueline, um his last uh and and longest-lasting muse of his life, um who he would marry about 5 years after this picture was painted.\" (≈25:30) [26:40–32:00] Company · Influence · Things - [≈26:42] He continued to develop on Cubism, working alongside Braque [music] on Analytic Cubism to Synthetic, effectively incorporating real-world materials into their artwork [music] to create depth in its messaging. - [≈29:05] His father was a great Anglophile and was known as El Inglés because of his passion for all things English and Picasso told [music] his biographer Roland Penrose that he was on his way to London in 1900 when he [music] stopped off in Paris and and never carri… - [≈29:47] &gt;&gt; There are about a dozen works by Picasso, including the most important, uh a portrait of Serge Lifar executed by Picasso in 1960, estimated [music] at uh 300 to 500,000 francs. - [≈30:24] This collaboration marked an important intersection of visual art, music, and dance, showcasing Picasso's innovative approach to stage design, and his influence on","t0":680,"t1":1360,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"17":0.07917513163643194,"18":0.04887457975802965,"19":0.04423107278812281,"20":0.03230403337118002,"21":0.040936452161504724,"22":0.05681270735455456,"23":0.0977491595160593,"24":0.04887457975802965,"25":0.08846214557624563,"26":0.14662373927408895,"29":0.08846214557624563,"30":0.11514283760214801,"32":0.08493138674210791,"36":0.04423107278812281,"39":0.052169200384647715,"40":0.07917513163643194,"42":0.04246569337105396,"46":0.04631907346390758,"47":0.04887457975802965,"52":0.08493138674210791,"54":0.04631907346390758,"56":0.04631907346390758,"300":0.04423107278812281,"500":0.04246569337105396,"1895":0.04887457975802965,"1900":0.04631907346390758,"1908