nd the… - [≈36:27] It's estimated at around $140 million, which is which in itself is already the most expensive work of art ever sold at auction. - [≈37:08] When a major work of art by a major artist comes up, There's sufficient global interest and the various economies are still strong enough to mean that they're pushed to to price levels which we haven't seen before. QUOTE: \"When a major work of art by a major artist comes up, There's sufficient global interest and the various economies are still strong enough to mean that they're pushed to to price levels which we haven't seen before.\" (≈37:08) [37:20–42:40] War · Guernica · Spanish - [≈39:21] Though he was being watched, the artist continued to resist [music] alongside his fellow Parisians, signing partitions against fascism and oppression, and taking part in secret resistance gatherings who were opposed to the Nazi atrocities. - [≈40:12] He never visited Guernica itself, the Basque town obliterated by German bombers in the Spanish Civil War. - [≈40:40] Measuring 3.49 m tall and 7.76 m wide, the painting is rendered in a stark monochromatic palette of black, white, and grays, which enhances [music] its dramatic impact and evokes the feel of newspaper photographs, contemporary accounts of the bombing, and per… - [≈41:29] Initially [music] displayed at the Spanish Pavilion of the 1937 World's Fair in Paris, it became a touring [music] exhibition to raise awareness and funds for Spanish war relief. QUOTE: \"He never visited Guernica itself, the Basque town obliterated by German bombers in the Spanish Civil War.\" (≈40:12) [42:40–45:47] Career · Death · Just - [≈42:44] This was one of 120 figures he created, [music] most of which featured nude females, with some animals such as owls, bulls, and monkeys, &gt;&gt; [music] [music] &gt;&gt; Pablo Picasso [music] produced around 13,500 paintings in his impressive 78-year career. - [≈44:01] The show of late Picasso at the Tate offers a careful [music] selection from the last 20 years of his life, from 1953 to '73. - [≈44:21] \"If I spit,\" he said, \"they'll take it, frame it, and sell it as great art.\" &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Picasso died at the Mas Notre Dame de Vie in Mougins on the 8th of April, 1978. - [≈44:48] He didn't just do paintings, so it's basically always","t0":1361,"t1":2041,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"12":0.06871617657597513,"13":0.034358088287987566,"14":0.03647557098802389,"20":0.08929380006646771,"21":0.07543684164221746,"27":0.03647557098802389,"29":0.08150809993057218,"32":0.039127447750242565,"35":0.09006505788509657,"36":0.04075404996528609,"37":0.19227263234690248,"39":0.04806815808672562,"40":0.25532899691616723,"41":0.04806815808672562,"42":0.1173823432507277,"44":0.18013011577019314,"45":0.04075404996528609,"47":0.09006505788509657,"48":0.039127447750242565,"49":0.045032528942548285,"56":0.042677912049213056,"73":0.04806815808672562,"76":0.04806815808672562,"78":0.04806815808672562,"80":0.04806815808672562,"120":0.04806815808672562,"140":0.04806815808672562,"300":0.04075404996528609,"500":0.07825489550048513,"1937":0.045032528942548285,"1953":0.04806815808672562,"1955":0.045032528942548285,"1960":0.039127447750242565,"1978":0.042677912049213056,"avant":0.039127447750242565,"garde":0.039127447750242565,"performance":0.04075404996528609,"art":0.10237515278707765,"quote":0.08748438859975305,"gt":0.23540774339216802,"there":0.041065901309798605,"dozen":0.042677912049213056,"works":0.026125833722406996,"picasso":0.1550123022981978,"including":0.03647557098802389,"most":0.0752469024038698,"important":0.054087960333096034,"uh":0.04095006111483106,"portrait":0.034358088287987566,"serge":0.042677912049213056,"lifar":0.042677912049213056,"executed":0.042677912049213056,"estimated":0.08150809993057218,"music":0.3018153602186814,"000":0.029764600022155904,"francs":0.042677912049213056,"00":0.03343994184384654,"looking":0.08113194049964405,"studies":0.14420447426017688,"color":0.10031982553153962,"he":0.099708