042677912049213056,"paintings":0.05718188812012629,"impressive":0.04806815808672562,"year":0.029161462866584345,"01":0.045032528942548285,"show":0.024882983889322155,"late":0.03771842082110873,"tate":0.045032528942548285,"offers":0.04806815808672562,"careful":0.04806815808672562,"selection":0.04806815808672562,"last":0.028049695806333978,"years":0.021558240015620102,"life":0.019033881754114405,"spit":0.045032528942548285,"said":0.019972458073979595,"ll":0.02100274189137241,"take":0.023425217716420896,"frame":0.04075404996528609,"sell":0.028590944060063146,"great":0.021276835938623603,"died":0.039127447750242565,"mas":0.045032528942548285,"notre":0.045032528942548285,"dame":0.045032528942548285,"de":0.03536380392777352,"vie":0.045032528942548285,"mougins":0.045032528942548285,"8th":0.04075404996528609,"april":0.04075404996528609,"didn":0.025281220868634605,"basically":0.03647557098802389,"always":0.024882983889322155}},{"id":"doc_1787410478461_jpjk55_c3","text":"constructions, going into ceramics. QUOTE: \"\"If I spit,\" he said, \"they'll take it, frame it, and sell it as great art.\" &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Picasso died at the Mas Notre Dame de Vie in Mougins on the 8th of April, 1978.\" (≈44:21) TAKEAWAYS & HEURISTICS: - &gt;&gt; Just off 5th Avenue, on a site long occupied by the old-fashioned town dwellings of the Rockefeller family, stands the spanking new home of a nationally important institution, the New York Museum of Modern Art. - His father was a great Anglophile and was known as El Inglés because of his passion for all things English and Picasso told [music] his biographer Roland Penrose that he was on his way to London in 1900 when he [music]… - Though he was being watched, the artist continued to resist [music] alongside his fellow Parisians, signing partitions against fascism and oppression, and taking part in secret resistance gatherings who were opposed to… - &gt;&gt; Well, we knew when it was bought that there was something on the &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; back, but we didn't know how important, how brilliant a picture it was until we removed the backing of the frame and sa… - &gt;&gt; There are about a dozen works by Picasso, including the most important, uh a portrait of Serge Lifar executed by Picasso in 1960, estimated [music] at uh 300 to 500,000 francs. NOTABLE QUOTES: - [≈2:35] \"In 1892, Picasso [music] began studying at the School of Fine Arts in La Coruña, where his father Don José taught.\" - [≈5:25] \"The two settled in a vacant studio whilst attending exhibitions such as the Universal, which raked in over 32 million visitors, all pining to see [music] the next influx of creative talent.\" - [≈13:52] \"Gertrude sat for hours in a broken arm chair in her home number 27 Rue de Fleurus.\" - [≈17:52] \"&gt;&gt; Just off 5th Avenue, on a site long occupied by the old-fashioned town dwellings of the Rockefeller family, stands the spanking new home of a nationally important institution, the New York Museum of Modern Art.\" - [≈25:30] \"It's very much a a paean to uh to Jacqueline, um his last uh and and longest-lasting muse of his life, um who he would marry about 5 years after this picture was painted.\" - [≈29:47] \"&gt;&gt; There are about a dozen works by Picasso, including the most important, uh a portrait of Serge Lifar executed by Picasso in 1960, estimated [music] at uh 300 to 500,000 francs.\" - [≈37:08] \"When a major work of art by a major artist comes up, There's sufficient global interest and the various economies are still strong enough to mean that they're pushed to to price levels which we haven't seen before.\" - [≈40:12] \"He never visited Guernica itself, the Basque town obliterated by German bombers in the Spanish Civil War.\" QUESTIONS THIS ANSWERS: - What does the source teach about gt? - What does the source teach about music? - What does the source","t0":2041,"t1":2721,"tsReal":false,"tfIdfVector":{"12":0.039928408620320745,"13":0.039928408620320745,"17":0.04238918914410415,"21"